	<!--Periwood Tricaster-->

	<ThingDef ParentName="BaseWildTerraweapon">
		<defName>ET_PeriwoodTricaster</defName>
		<label>Periwood Tricaster</label>
		<description>The Tricaster is the second iteration of the experimental "caster" weapon type, which was meant as a heirarchy of "staple" weapons that Terratech tribes could always rely on. This specific iteration introduces multiple traits of the Periwood line, though there are some notable differences due to it's method of acquisition.
Created by combining a Primcaster with a Periwood Heart at a Biosynth Vat.
\n\nThe "Caster" line is a special weapon that does not belong to one genome; rather, it is evolved directly into other ones to take on new traits, while maintaining previous ones. These weapons often outperform other weapons in their same tier, but creating them take significant time and investment.
The Tricaster features the following bonuses and penalties:
-Stage 2 out of ?
-"Pure" Form: The Tricaster can be further evolved
-Prima Bonus: The Tricaster can accept advanced saps
-Prima Bonus: The Tricaster produces a special seed upon expiry
-Periwood Bonus (NEW): The Tricaster has a drastically extended lifespan
-Periwood Bonus (NEW): The Tricaster can be replanted to be regrown
-Periwood Handicap (NEW): Sap infusion requires special means due to sap inaccesibility</description>
